Translation patch: <Scalar as Product<T>>::product (src/scalar.rs)

Change: `iter.fold(Scalar::ONE, |acc, item| acc * item.borrow())` becomes a `while let` loop
accumulating `acc = acc * item.borrow()`.

Why: the Aeneas Lean library models only `Iterator::next`; the provided
methods (`map`, `zip`, `fold`, `filter`, `collect`, `rev`/`skip` on adapters, ...)
are missing (AeneasVerif/aeneas#1057), so the original does not build in Lean.

Behaviour: identical: `fold` is defined as exactly this loop over `next()`.

Remove this patch when Aeneas translates the original code: delete the file,
run ./scripts/aeneas-translate.sh and `lake build`, and check both succeed.

diff --git a/curve25519-dalek/src/scalar.rs b/curve25519-dalek/src/scalar.rs
index c417780..99e9364 100644
--- a/curve25519-dalek/src/scalar.rs
+++ b/curve25519-dalek/src/scalar.rs
@@ -457,11 +457,15 @@ impl<T> Product<T> for Scalar
 where
     T: Borrow<Scalar>,
 {
-    fn product<I>(iter: I) -> Self
+    fn product<I>(mut iter: I) -> Self
     where
         I: Iterator<Item = T>,
     {
-        iter.fold(Scalar::ONE, |acc, item| acc * item.borrow())
+        let mut acc = Scalar::ONE;
+        while let Some(item) = iter.next() {
+            acc = acc * item.borrow();
+        }
+        acc
     }
 }
 
